libsurface (0.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * packaging: floors and ceilings on libdiginet and libmackie, 0.2.2
    changelog
  * tests: netns.h copied from libdiginet 0.1.8
  * emu-sync-check: accept libdiginet's testsupport/ layout
  * tests: leave the public-sources check to the shared one
  * tests: a check that reads no file is red
  * ci: test_c24_tool runs on the runner, and a skip there fails the job
  * tests/diginet: the probe and the floors follow emu_child.h
  * tests/diginet: test_c24_tool runs on libdiginet-emu's child harness
  * release: libsurface 0.2.2
  * ci: the modules build on libdiginet's and libmackie's dedupe/all in a
    dedupe/all run
  * packaging: every package installs its licence and the short README
  * packaging: no markdown in the packages; their descriptions name
    openmixer.org
  * tests: the local public-sources check gives way to the shared one
  * ci: the shared checks run from FreeMixer/.github's public-sources-check
  * test: no-emu-copy-sabotage.sh lists an unpacked tarball without git
  * test: no-emu-copy-sabotage.sh in an unpacked tarball against an installed
    emulator
  * diginet tests: build against libdiginet-emu, the desk emulator libdiginet
    installs
  * test: no file defines libdiginet's desk emulator again (no-emu-copy.sh,
    with its sabotage)
  * tests: libdiginet's desk emulator copied again from its main (fc831ee,
    after #56)
  * README: the Mackie module exists, only the Python binding is later

